Add the FajitaRtc built-in personality: the PM8998 RTC driver (drivers/FajitaRtc) matches the
/arm-io/rtc nub of the ADT (make-fajita-adt.py --rtc, compatible qcom,pm8941-rtc) and serves the
wall clock as the IORTC resource. Unconditional, like the NativeDwc3 one: without the FajitaRtc
archive IOKit finds no such class, and without the ADT node there is no nub to match. Applies after
zzv-native-dwc3-personality.patch, whose block it follows; the kernel script reverses it first
(LATE list of scripts/build-xnu-4k-baseline.sh).
diff --git a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
--- a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
+++ b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
@@ -106,4 +106,11 @@
     "     'IOProviderClass' = IOPlatformExpertDevice;"
     "     'IOProbeScore'    = 400:32;"
     "   }"
+    "   ,{"
+    "     'IOClass'         = FajitaRtc;"
+    "     'IOMatchCategory' = FajitaRtc;"
+    "     'IOProviderClass' = IOPlatformDevice;"
+    "     'IONameMatch'     = 'qcom,pm8941-rtc';"
+    "     'IOProbeScore'    = 1000:32;"
+    "   }"
     ")";
